---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const issueUrl =
  'https://github.com/govtech-bb/govbb-design-system/issues/new/choose';
const repositoryUrl =
  'https://github.com/govtech-bb/govbb-design-system';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support and governance"
  section="support"
  description="Get help, report an issue and understand how the GovBB Design System is maintained."
>
  <section class="govbb-width-container govbb-page-section">
    <div class="govbb-page-header">
      <h1 class="govbb-page-title">Support and governance</h1>
      <p class="govbb-page-subtitle">
        Get help using the system, report a problem and understand how guidance
        is maintained.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="govbb-prose">
      <h2>Get help</h2>
      <p>
        Start with the <a href="/documentation/">adoption guidance</a> and
        search the component, pattern and template references. Every reference
        page links to its source and raw Markdown.
      </p>

      <h2>Report an issue</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={issueUrl}>Open an issue on GitHub</a> for incorrect guidance,
        accessibility barriers, broken examples or missing use cases. Do not
        include personal, confidential or security-sensitive information in a
        public issue.
      </p>

      <h2>Contribute</h2>
      <p>
        The GovBB Design System team maintains the published packages and this
        documentation. Review the <a href={repositoryUrl}>source repository</a>
        and open an issue before proposing a substantial change so the user need
        and affected services can be agreed first.
      </p>

      <h2>How decisions are recorded</h2>
      <p>
        Significant design decisions are published in the
        <a href="/design-log/">design log</a>. Issues are triaged by the
        maintainers; response times depend on severity and available capacity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
